.Dd September 25, 2026
.Dt PAZARID.TOML 5
.Os pazari
.Sh NAME
.Nm pazarid.toml
.Nd configuration file for pazarid
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Xr pazarid 1
reads its configuration from a TOML file,
.Pa /etc/pazari/pazarid.toml
by default.
.Ql pazarid example-config
prints a complete file with every key at its default.
.Pp
Sizes and durations are written as in
.Xr pazari-agent.toml 5 .
Unless stated otherwise, a duration must be greater than zero and at most 24
hours.
.Sh SETTINGS
.Ss Top level
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm tick_interval No = Ar duration
How often the daemon re-reads host memory, checks on pending resizes and quiet
guests, and updates its metrics.
Default
.Cm 1s .
.El
.Ss [policy]
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm host_floor No = Ar size
Memory the host keeps for itself.
A grow is granted only if available memory stays at or above this afterwards.
Required; may be 0.
.It Cm grant_swap No = Ar boolean
Whether free swap counts as available memory.
Default
.Cm false .
.It Cm grant_min_interval No = Ar duration
Minimum time between grants to one guest.
Also the retry delay given with
.Cm host_pressure
refusals.
Default
.Cm 5s .
.It Cm reconcile_deadline No = Ar duration
How long a resize may take before the daemon stops waiting for it.
Default
.Cm 30s .
.It Cm shrink_revert No = Ar boolean
Whether a shrink that did not finish is reverted to the size the guest actually
holds.
Default
.Cm true .
.It Cm welcome_status_interval No = Ar duration
How often guests must report their status.
Default
.Cm 1s .
.It Cm stale_after No = Ar count
How many status intervals a guest may miss before it is marked stale.
Default
.Cm 3 .
.It Cm reclaim_deadline No = Ar duration
How long a guest has to answer a reclaim request.
Default
.Cm 30s .
.El
.Ss [policy.revocation]
Optional.
Without it, the daemon never asks guests to return memory, except after a
ceiling is lowered.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm psi No = Ar percent
Host memory pressure, as
.Va some avg10 ,
at which to start asking.
Greater than 0 and at most 100.
Required.
.It Cm step No = Ar size
How much to ask for at a time.
Default
.Cm 256MiB .
.El
.Pp
On each tick where host pressure is at or above
.Cm psi ,
the daemon asks the guest holding the most memory above its boot size for
.Cm step ,
or for that excess if it is smaller.
One guest is asked per tick.
.Ss [metrics]
Optional.
Without it, the daemon serves no metrics.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm listen No = Ar address
Address to serve OpenMetrics on, for example
.Ql 127.0.0.1:9650 .
Required.
.El
.Ss [guests.<name>]
One table per guest.
.Ar name
is used in logs and as the
.Va guest
metric label.
At least one guest is required.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm ceiling No = Ar size
The most memory the guest may have, counting boot memory and plugged memory.
Required.
.El
.Ss [guests.<name>.transport]
How the guest connects.
Required.
Two guests cannot share a context ID or socket path.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm kind No = Qq Cm vsock
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm cid No = Ar integer
The guest's context ID, which identifies it.
Required.
.It Cm port No = Ar integer
The port the guest connects to.
Default
.Cm 4650 .
.El
.It Cm kind No = Qq Cm unix
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm path No = Ar path
The socket the guest connects to.
Any existing file at this path is removed.
Required.
.El
.El
.Ss [guests.<name>.qmp]
The hypervisor's QMP socket and the guest's memory device.
Required.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm path No = Ar path
The QMP socket.
Required.
.It Cm device No = Ar id
The
.Va id
of the guest's virtio-mem device.
Required.
.It Cm deadline No = Ar duration
Timeout for a single QMP command.
Default
.Cm 5s .
.It Cm retry_min No = Ar duration
First delay before reconnecting to a device that stopped answering.
Default
.Cm 500ms .
.It Cm retry_max No = Ar duration
Maximum reconnect delay; the delay doubles up to this.
Must be at least
.Cm retry_min .
Default
.Cm 30s .
.El
.Ss [guests.<name>.qmp.mode]
Optional; defaults to
.Cm held .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm kind No = Qq Cm held
Keep one connection open and learn of resizes from QMP events.
.It Cm kind No = Qq Cm per_operation
Open a connection per command, for a socket shared with other tools.
Resizes are polled for.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm poll No = Ar duration
Polling interval during a resize.
Default
.Cm 1s .
.El
.El
.Sh CAPACITY
The daemon warns at startup if
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sum(ceilings) + host_floor > MemTotal + SwapTotal
.Ed
.Pp
but starts anyway, since guests rarely all reach their ceilings at once.
To guarantee that every byte a guest can hold is RAM, set ceilings so that
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sum(ceilings) + host_floor <= MemTotal
.Ed
.Pp
The daemon does not limit how much of the host one guest can take below its
ceiling.
Under
.Cm grant_swap = true
in particular, one guest can use up the free swap.
Set a memory limit on each VM's own systemd unit on the host.
.Sh METRICS
With
.Cm [metrics]
configured, the daemon publishes the following, each prefixed
.Ql pazarid_ .
Gauges are updated once per tick.
.Ss Per-guest gauges
Labelled
.Va guest .
.Bl -tag -width "guest_reclaim_outstanding" -compact
.It Va guest_size_bytes
Current size of the guest's memory device.
.It Va guest_ceiling_bytes
The guest's ceiling.
.It Va guest_connected
1 while the guest is connected.
.It Va guest_stale
1 while the guest is stale.
.It Va guest_reclaim_outstanding
1 while a reclaim request awaits an answer.
.El
.Ss Host gauges
.Bl -tag -width "guest_reclaim_outstanding" -compact
.It Va host_available_bytes
.Va MemAvailable .
.It Va host_swap_free_bytes
.Va SwapFree .
.It Va host_psi
Host memory pressure,
.Va some avg10 .
.El
.Ss Counters
.Bl -tag -width "device_refused_actuations_total" -compact
.It Va connections_total
Guest connections accepted.
.It Va disconnections_total
Guest connections lost.
.It Va closes_total
Connections closed by the daemon.
.It Va grants_total
Grants issued.
.It Va denies_total
Refusals, labelled
.Va reason .
.It Va reclaim_requests_total
Reclaim requests sent.
.It Va guest_messages_total
Messages received, labelled
.Va kind .
.It Va device_reconnects_total
Per guest: reconnections to the memory device.
.It Va device_seed_failures_total
Per guest: failures to read the device's size on connecting.
.It Va device_refused_actuations_total
Per guest: resizes the hypervisor refused.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/pazari/pazarid.toml
Default configuration file.
.It Pa share/doc/pazari/examples/pazarid.toml
Annotated example, installed with the package.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
A host keeping 4GiB for itself, asking for memory back under pressure, with one
guest:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
tick_interval = "1s"

[policy]
host_floor = "4GiB"
grant_min_interval = "5s"
grant_swap = false

[policy.revocation]
psi = 20.0
step = "256MiB"

[metrics]
listen = "127.0.0.1:9650"

[guests.example]
ceiling = "32GiB"

[guests.example.transport]
kind = "vsock"
cid = 3

[guests.example.qmp]
path = "/run/pazari/example.qmp"
device = "vm0"
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pazari-agent 1 ,
.Xr pazarid 1 ,
.Xr qemu 1 ,
.Xr pazari-agent.toml 5 ,
.Xr proc 5 ,
.Xr pazari 7
